<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thirteen Years' War (1454–1466)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1454">1454</a>–<a href="/years/1466">1466</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as War of the Cities</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thirteen Years' War (1454–1466) was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a>, allied with the Prussian Confederation of towns and nobles, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>. It began when the Prussian estates rebelled against the Order and placed themselves under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-iv-jagiellon">Casimir IV Jagiellon</a>. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-peace-of-thorn">Second Peace of Thorn</a> (1466) <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> gained Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, including Danzig and the Order's capital Marienburg, while the Order kept eastern Prussia as a Polish fief.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thirteen-years-war-1454-1466.jpg" alt="Thirteen Years' War (1454–1466)" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polish_Knights_1447-1492.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
